Landing zone for developer documentation of btrfs
-------------------------------------------------

Before this will be public, we want to have some example chapters with basic
structure and formatting.

* collect your notes about an area you understand, have reviewed or have documented already
* start a whole structure of the docs, chapters, sections, ...
* skip formatting for now
* document how things are implemented, the main areas, operations
* high-level overview

Examples in no particular order:

* mount
* physical and logical addressing (aka. chunk tree mappings)
* how balance, scrub, dev-replace work
* purpose of various trees
* data structures
* transaction commit phases
* compression write out
* space reservations
* connections to VFS: acl, xattr, inode, file
* MM: pagecache
* locking
* backreferences
* free space tracking
* tree-log
* subvolumes from the inside, radix tree, dentry lookups
* ioctl interface
* delayed refs
* delayed inodes
* workqueues
* orphans

Repository workflow:
* clone your version
* start a new document or edit existing
* send merge request
* repeat
